  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "$\\int {5}^{-x}\\,\\text{d}x=$",
  "worked_solution": "If we let $u=-x$, then \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-1\\,\u27f9\\,-\\text{d}u=\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nThen, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {5}^{-x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {5}^{u}\\cdot (-1)\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\int {5}^{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{{5}^{u}}{\\operatorname{ln}\u20615}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{{5}^{-x}}{\\operatorname{ln}\u20615}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$",
